# Build-time configuration for the production site.
#
# Committed on purpose. A GA4 measurement ID is not a secret: it ships inside
# the page and anyone can read it. Keeping it here rather than in a shell
# variable removes the one failure mode that matters, which is a release built
# without it. That build is not broken, it just quietly stops counting, and the
# privacy notice correctly stops mentioning analytics, so nothing on screen
# tells you the release was wrong.
#
# To turn analytics off, delete the line. Do not set it to an empty string in
# one place and a real value in another.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-M4VRDKT4YE
